# Deliberate binary breaks in 1.10.0, relative to 1.9.0. See the release note in README.md.
#
# THESE FILTERS DO NOT RETIRE. sbt-mima reads every *.backwards.excludes in this directory
# whatever it is named, so this file stays in force until somebody deletes it. Delete it at the
# 1.10.0 post-release, when previousRelease moves to 1.10.0.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# #55: CameFromJournal gains a `keepFirst` field.
#
# All three breaks are one change: adding a parameter to a case class changes its constructor,
# its `copy` and its companion's `apply`. The field carries a default, so every source call site
# compiles unchanged -- this is source-compatible and binary-incompatible, and a caller needs a
# recompile rather than an edit.
#
# The field exists because a came-from map has to choose between the several vertices that can
# reach a node before it is visited, and THE TWO TRAVERSALS WANT OPPOSITE ANSWERS. Breadth-first
# wants the first, which is on a shortest path. Depth-first wants the last, which is the vertex it
# actually expands from, because that is the frame nearest the top of the stack. Through 1.9.x the
# journal always kept the first, so it was right for BFS and wrong for DFS.
#
# The behavioural change matters more than the binary one, and it is why this is 1.10.0 rather
# than 1.9.1: `withListJournalAndCameFrom` now returns a different map for the same traversal of
# the same graph. The old map was not the DFS tree. On a transitive tournament a DFS walking the
# path 0,1,2,3,4,5 reported a star rooted at 0, because every vertex really was first seen from
# the source -- the traversal had the right answer and the journal discarded it. BFS is unchanged.
#
# See #55, and rchillyard/Gryphon#144 where it surfaced.
#
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.CameFromJournal.this")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.CameFromJournal.copy")
ProblemFilters.exclude[DirectMissingMethodProblem]("com.phasmidsoftware.visitor.core.CameFromJournal.apply")
